## Test Plan

| Test Case | Input | Expected Result |
|-----------|-------|----------------|
| Valid message | `{"deviceId": "sensor_01", "ts": "1699900000", "reading": 23.5}` | Inserted into BigQuery |
| Missing deviceId | `{"ts": "1699900000", "reading": 23.5}` | Published to DLQ |
| Missing ts | `{"deviceId": "sensor_01", "reading": 23.5}` | Published to DLQ |
| Missing reading | `{"deviceId": "sensor_01", "ts": "1699900000"}` | Published to DLQ |
| Duplicate message | Same valid message sent twice | Only one record inserted (deduplicated via insertId) |

## Idempotency

The `insertId = deviceId + '_' + ts` ensures that duplicate messages within 24 hours are deduplicated by BigQuery, providing exactly-once semantics for the insert operation.

